# CVE-2026-14456: OpenSSL denial of service via unbounded memory growth in the
# QUIC server. Unlike every batch above this is an application library rather
# than a kernel header, and it is accepted on reachability rather than on the
# absence of a fix.
#
# Nojoin terminates no QUIC and serves no HTTP/3. The API is uvicorn over
# HTTP/1.1, the frontend is Next.js, and the bundled nginx declares no
# `listen ... quic` or `http3` directive on any server block, so the vulnerable
# server-side QUIC path is not reachable in any deployment this repository
# ships. An operator fronting Nojoin with their own HTTP/3 terminator is running
# that terminator's OpenSSL, not the one in these images.
#
# Reviewed 2026-09-17 ahead of v2.5.1. The Debian half has cleared: the api
# runtime stage now runs `apt-get upgrade`, which installs the patched openssl,
# and the api image scans clean with this entry removed. The entry stays for the
# frontend alone. Alpine needs 3.5.8-r0 and the pinned node:26-alpine (Alpine
# 3.24.1) still carries 3.5.7-r0. It clears on a node base rebuild, hence the
# short review date.
#   Owner: maintainers. Review by: 2026-10-15.
CVE-2026-14456

# CVE-2026-58659: PyTorch Lightning code execution through a checkpoint's
# `_instantiator` hyperparameter. A false positive against the pinned version,
# accepted because the advisory's version range is wrong and not because the
# risk is tolerated.
#
# The fix is upstream PR 21832, released in lightning 2.6.6, and
# requirements/worker.txt pins lightning and pytorch-lightning at 2.6.6. The
# allowlist it adds (`_ALLOWED_INSTANTIATORS` in lightning/pytorch/core/saving.py)
# was confirmed present in the 2.6.6 tag and in the installed package, and absent
# from 2.6.5.
#
# GHSA-qqmf-gpg7-g8gw records the affected range for `lightning` as
# `< 2022.6.15`. PyPI lists no such release, and every 2.x version sorts below
# it, so no upgrade can clear the finding. The PyPA record for the same CVE,
# PYSEC-2026-3624, gives the fix as 2.6.6, and OSV lists pytorch-lightning 2.6.6
# as unaffected. Trivy reads the GitHub range.
#
# This file matches on CVE id alone, so the entry would also mask a vulnerable
# copy if either pin were moved back below 2.6.6. Do not lower them. Remove the
# entry once the advisory database corrects the range.
#   Owner: maintainers. Review by: 2026-10-15.
CVE-2026-58659
